    "q-176831": {
      "dom_id": "step-q176831",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "The third term of the expression $8-\\frac{3}{4}a-\\frac{4}{5}b+2c$ is{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "We put an addition symbol $(+)$ between each part and separate using parentheses:\n\n$$\n(8)+(-\\frac{3}{4}a)+(-\\frac{4}{5}b)+(2c)\n$$\n\nCounting off the terms:\n\n- the first term is $8,$\n\n- the second term is $-\\frac{3}{4}a,$\n\n- the third term is $-\\frac{4}{5}b,$ and\n\n- the fourth term is $2c.$\n\nIn particular, we are interested in the third term. The third term is $-\\frac{4}{5}b.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
