    "q-67052": {
      "dom_id": "step-q67052",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "What is the fourth term of the expression $5a-\\frac{4}{3}b-12c+\\frac{1}{2}d?$",
      "worked_solution": "We put an addition symbol $(+)$ between each part and separate using parentheses:\n\n$$\n(5a)+(-\\frac{4}{3}b)+(-12c)+(\\frac{1}{2}d)\n$$\n\nCounting off the terms:\n\n- the first term is $5a,$\n\n- the second term is $-\\frac{4}{3}b,$\n\n- the third term is $-12c,$ and\n\n- the fourth term is $\\frac{1}{2}d.$\n\nIn particular, we are interested in the fourth term. The fourth term is $\\frac{1}{2}d.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
