    "q-43970": {
      "dom_id": "step-q43970",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "What's the third term of the expression $\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{2x}{7}-1.3z-6y?$",
      "worked_solution": "We put an addition symbol $(+)$ between each part and separate using parentheses:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{3}{2})+(\\frac{2x}{7})+(-1.3z)+(-6y)\n$$\n\nCounting off the terms:\n\n- the first term is $\\frac{3}{2},$\n\n- the second term is $\\frac{2x}{7},$\n\n- the third term is $-1.3z,$ and\n\n- the fourth term is $-6y.$\n\nIn particular, we are interested in the third term. The third term is $-1.3z.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
