    "q-174099": {
      "dom_id": "step-q174099",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "Create an expression equivalent to $3x-2y+4z-3w:$\n\n$3x-2y+4z-3w=$\n{{field-1}}\n$w\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$y\\,+$\n{{field-3}}\n$x\\,+$\n{{field-4}}\n$z$",
      "worked_solution": "The expression $3x-2y+4z-3w$ has four terms: $3x$, $-2y$, $4z$, and $-3w.$ \n\nThe order in which we combine the terms doesn't matter. Therefore, we can also write this expression as \n\n$$\n-3w-2y+3x+4z.\n$$",
